# The STAMPED a11y surface: these widgets are COPIES from a row template.
# IT MUST STAY ITS OWN SCENE — a For materializes as a COLUMN and
# container creation order differs by language, so a For added to
# a11y.steps would move that scene's ordinal container targets.
# THE IDS ARE ELEMENT-SOURCED: expect_ax searches the real tree BY
# IDENTIFIER and refuses copies sharing a const template id.
expect_ax entry#0 "field/First note"
expect_ax entry#last "field/Second note"
# THE STAMPED STYLING PROPS (docs/styling-plan.md D3/D4): `heading` is
# the role with a real-tree observable on every platform, read here off
# an element that was never authored, only stamped.
expect_ax label#0 "heading/Heading one"
expect_ax label#last "heading/Heading two"
# The stamped container's own padding, RELATIVE like styling.steps'
# window inset.
expect_inset row#0 8
